 - *Five-day hysteresis after a service breakdown.* On day 2 of a five-day horizon, metro line A fails at 17:00 and imposes a 45-minute delay; the network is nominal again from day 3. <!-- source: experiments.yaml, exp_04a perturbation --> Three conditions are compared: an agent with a short-term memory buffer in the sense of Park et al. (2023), decaying at rate λ; the same agent without memory; the tabular oracle, structurally memoryless. No survey follows the same travellers through such an event, so no value is a target. What is testable is the order of the conditions on day 3, **[xx.y | exp_04a vs exp_04b vs exp_04c]**, the monotonic recovery over days 3 to 5, and the displacement of the curve when λ is divided by three, **[xx.y | exp_04d]**. The hypothesis falls if the memoryless agent shows the same inertia, if λ has no effect, or if recovery is not monotonic.
-- *Five real, dated local news events.* Five real, dated articles of the Toulouse local press, chosen before any model call, provide five events. <!-- source: RAPPORT_SCENARIOS_QUALITATIFS_TOULOUSE.md §2 and §3 --> Each acts through a distinct channel, and none is representable as a tabular variable: gusts of the Autan wind above 80 km/h closing the city's parks, a weather and physical-safety channel at metropolitan scale; a bed-bug scare in the metro and buses, a perceived-risk channel at network scale; an open-ended strike of waste collectors in the historic centre, a sensory-nuisance channel at district scale; the street parade of La Machine with a pedestrianised centre, a closure-and-attraction channel on the centre and its radial axes; the launch of electric bike-sharing on the hilly districts, a supply channel at metropolitan scale. Articles the grid discarded provide the placebo condition. Each event is run under five conditions on the same personas: nominal, raw article, mode-neutral paraphrase that removes every mention of a mode, placebo article, and the tabular oracle with the event encoded into its variables where the event admits such an encoding. For each event and each mode, the expected direction of the shift was written down before any model call, 20 signed predictions in all; we report the share of observed modal shifts that go in the expected direction **[xx.y | exp_05]**, with option order randomised for every request as SILICA recommends (Bin Tareaf, 2026). The raw-minus-paraphrase contrast isolates instruction following from reasoning; the placebo contrast isolates specificity.
+- *Five real, dated local news events.* Five real, dated articles of the Toulouse local press, chosen before any model call, provide five events. <!-- source: RAPPORT_SCENARIOS_QUALITATIFS_TOULOUSE.md §2 and §3 --> Each acts through a distinct channel, and none is representable as a tabular variable: gusts of the Autan wind above 80 km/h closing the city's parks, a weather and physical-safety channel at metropolitan scale; a bed-bug scare in the metro and buses, a perceived-risk channel at network scale; an open-ended strike of waste collectors in the historic centre, a sensory-nuisance channel at district scale; the street parade of La Machine with a pedestrianised centre, a closure-and-attraction channel on the centre and its radial axes; the launch of electric bike-sharing on the hilly districts, a supply channel at metropolitan scale. Each event is run under five conditions on the same personas: the nominal day, with no article; the raw article; a mode-neutral paraphrase, the same fact rewritten without any mention of a mode; a neutral control text, a real local article of similar length with no plausible link to mode choice, which measures the effect of adding any text at all; and the tabular oracle with the event encoded into its variables where the event admits such an encoding. For each event and each mode, the expected direction of the shift was written down before any model call, 20 signed predictions in all; we report the share of observed modal shifts that go in the expected direction **[xx.y | exp_05]**, with option order randomised for every request as SILICA recommends (Bin Tareaf, 2026). The raw-minus-paraphrase contrast isolates instruction following from reasoning; the contrast with the neutral control text separates the effect of the article's content from the effect of adding a text.
 
